  "generated_text": "1. Let the length of a side of the square be \\( s \\) inches.\n2. The perimeter of the square is given by \\( 4s \\) inches.\n3. The area of the square is given by \\( s^2 \\) square inches.\n4. According to the problem, the perimeter is equal to the area:\n   \\[\n   4s = s^2\n   \\]\n5. To solve for \\( s \\), we rearrange the equation:\n   \\[\n   s^2 - 4s = 0\n   \\]\n6. Factor out \\( s \\):\n   \\[\n   s(s - 4) = 0\n   \\]\n7. This gives us two solutions:\n   \\[\n   s = 0 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad s = 4\n   \\]\n8. Since \\( s \\) represents the length of a side of a square, it must be a positive value. Therefore, we discard \\( s = 0 \\).\n\nThus, the length of a side of the square is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{4}\n\\]",
